# This project has no build step and no dependencies — it runs straight from
# index.html. There is very little to ignore.

# Editor / OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Local tooling config (machine-specific paths)
.claude/

# Logs and temp files
*.log
*.tmp

# --- machine learning ------------------------------------------------------
# The synthetic population is large and fully regenerable from a seed:
#   python ml/generate_population.py --n 8000 --years 14
# The seed is fixed, so anyone can reproduce the exact training set.
# The population is 37 MB and fully regenerable from a fixed seed:
#   python ml/generate_population.py --n 40000 --years 16
# Its income levels are calibrated to the CBDT published distribution, so the
# generated file is reproducible rather than arbitrary - ml/calibration.py
# holds the targets and ml/validate_population.py checks the match.
ml/data/*.csv
# ...but the sample and the data dictionary ARE committed, so that anyone
# opening the repository can see what the data looks like without having to
# regenerate 38 MB first. The sample is drawn by whole career rather than by
# row, so it carries the same income distribution as the full population.
!ml/data/population_sample.csv
!ml/data/DATA_DICTIONARY.csv
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# models/forecaster.json IS committed on purpose. The app is client-side with
# no build step, so the trained model has to ship with it — a visitor cannot
# run Python to produce one. ml/data/export_check.json ships with it so the
# cross-language test can run anywhere.
